{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Sarah denied, saying.</b> From here [we learn] that women are disqualified from testimony, because they deny out of fear." "<b>For she was afraid.</b> Some interpret: every כי in the Torah is translated ארי (that is, 'indeed/because'), for just as the word כי in the holy language serves four functions — for if you should say it is translated כי יקרא אי (if, perhaps), and כי תאמר דלמא (if, perhaps), and כי צחקת אלא (but rather), and כי יראה דהא (because, indeed), and the others ארי (because) — then there are five functions in the word כי. Therefore all of them are translated ארי, except that in four places the translator showed you the sense."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "The comment enumerates five functions but introduces the list saying 'four'; this appears to reflect the received text as written. The Aramaic translation words (אי, דלמא, אלא, דהא, ארי) are cited from Onkelos's renderings of כי in various verses."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:45.138736757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}